# Recommends, not Depends, on the two RTS2 packages: rts2-httpd and
# rts2-jsonclient link base_kernel and db statically (`ldd` shows no
# rts2 shared object at all), so nothing here needs those packages
# present to install or to run. What the daemon needs is a *running*
# RTS2 system to talk to and, with WEB_WITH_DB, a database - and a site
# may well have those from a source build rather than from these
# packages. That is exactly the D50 case as of 2026-08-31: rts2-httpd is
# wanted there before the rest of the port has been deployed, and a hard
# Depends would have made that impossible without --force-depends.
Recommends: rts2-base,
            rts2-db
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Remote Telescope System 2 - HTTP/JSON API daemon and dashboard
 RTS2 (Remote Telescope System, 2nd version) is a distributed control
 system for robotic astronomical observatories.
 .
 This package contains rts2-httpd, the daemon exposing the RTS2 device bus
 and observation database to the outside world over HTTP: a JSON/REST API,
 live value and state push over WebSocket, FITS image previews, and
 target/observation history. It also ships the static dashboard served
 from /usr/share/rts2-web/static, and rts2-jsonclient, the command line
 client for that API (the scriptable replacement for classic's
 rts2-xmlrpcclient).
 .
 This is a from-scratch redesign of classic src/httpd rather than a
 mechanical port - see web/STATUS.md in the source tree for the rationale.
 Built with WEB_WITH_DB=ON, so the target/observation history endpoints
 are compiled in and rts2-db is required; the daemon still starts and
 serves its non-DB endpoints when the database is unreachable at runtime.
